# Taigam, Master Opportunist: on turn three Taigam is Bot1's first spell of the turn, so Lightning Bolt, cast once Taigam is in play,
# is the second and flurry triggers (the Mox cast on turn one is a spell of that earlier turn). The copy is made first (CR 707.10)
# and resolves before the original, dealing 3 to Bot2. Then the original is exiled with four time counters, so it never
# resolves, and gains suspend (CR 702.62a): a counter comes off at each of Bot1's upkeeps (turns 5, 7, 9, 11) and when the last is gone
# Bot1 may cast it without paying its mana cost, so the exiled Bolt itself deals 3 more.

